  "full_text": "Loot chest\n\nIntroduction. A loot chest functions like regular chest, but is spawned at World Creation at a certain point of interest and contains loot appropriate to the biome where it appears, and sometimes treasure than can be used to barter with Haldor.\n\nTroll Cave Chest. There could be more than 1 chest in the cave\nAlso there's loot on the floor:\nUp to 9 treasures with 50% spawn each containing one of:\n• 1-3 Amber pearl\n• 1-2 Ruby\n• 1-5 Amber\n• 5-20 Coins\nUp to 12 Yellow mushrooms with 50% chance each.\nUp to 3 Bone fragments (at the entrance) with 66% chance each.\n\nShipwreck Chest. Note: Since chest spawn not more than one of each option, it's impossible to get 4, so if random check rolls 4, all 3 of them spawns.\n\nSwamp Chest. Located in Abandoned Hut and Swamp Runestone Tower.\n\nMountain Chest. Located in Abandoned Cabin, Mountain Tower and Mountain's Inverted Tower.\n\nFrost Cave Chest. In addition to treasure chests, rooms in frost caves may contain meat piles. Each meat pile will drop 1 Entrail, and 50% of the time it will also drop:\n\nPlains Chest. Located in Fuling Village, Fuling Outpost and Fuling Ruin.\n\nInfested Mine Treasure Chest. There are two kinds of treasure room inside Infested Mines:\nEach treasure chest holds the following:\nEach coin pile will drop 1 Coin in addition to:",
